### Exercise 4: Boot Troubleshooting (5 min)

**Task:** Practice rescue mode and boot analysis.

\`\`\`bash
# 1. Analyze current boot
systemd-analyze
systemd-analyze blame | head -20
systemd-analyze critical-chain

# 2. Generate boot visualization
systemd-analyze plot > /tmp/boot.svg
# Open boot.svg in browser to visualize

# 3. Check for failed services
systemctl --failed

# 4. Practice entering rescue mode (CAREFUL!)
# DON'T RUN IN PRODUCTION!
# sudo systemctl rescue
# (requires root password, type 'exit' to return)

# 5. Review boot logs
journalctl -b | less
journalctl -b -p err  # Errors only

# 6. Check kernel messages
journalctl -k -b

# 7. Practice GRUB editing (READ ONLY)
# sudo grubby --info=ALL
# sudo grubby --info=DEFAULT
\`\`\`

