        content: `
## SELinux — Security Enhanced Linux

### Modes

\`\`\`bash
# Check status
getenforce
sestatus

# Modes:
# - Enforcing: blocks and logs
# - Permissive: logs only
# - Disabled: completely off

# Temporary change
setenforce 0    # permissive
setenforce 1    # enforcing

# Permanent: /etc/selinux/config
SELINUX=enforcing
\`\`\`

### Contexts

\`\`\`bash
# View context
ls -Z /var/www/html
ps auxZ | grep httpd

# Context format: user:role:type:level
# system_u:object_r:httpd_sys_content_t:s0

# Change context
chcon -t httpd_sys_content_t /var/www/html/index.html

# Restore default
restorecon -Rv /var/www/html
\`\`\`

### Booleans

\`\`\`bash
# List booleans
getsebool -a | grep httpd

# Set boolean (temporary)
setsebool httpd_can_network_connect on

# Set boolean (persistent)
setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect on
\`\`\`

### Troubleshooting

\`\`\`bash
# View denials
ausearch -m avc -ts recent
grep denied /var/log/audit/audit.log

# Generate policy
audit2why < /var/log/audit/audit.log
\`\`\`
        `,
        keyPoints: [
          "getenforce/setenforce — status va mode",
          "chcon — context o'zgartirish",
          "restorecon — default context",
          "setsebool -P — persistent boolean"
        ]
      },
      {
        id: 2,
        title: "SSH & Firewall Security",
        type: "theory",
        duration: "40 min",
        content: `
## SSH & Firewall Security Best Practices

### SSH Hardening

#### /etc/ssh/sshd_config - Critical Settings

\`\`\`bash
# Disable root login
PermitRootLogin no

# Key-only authentication
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PermitEmptyPasswords no

# User restrictions
AllowUsers admin deploy
AllowGroups sshusers

# Network
Port 2222
AddressFamily inet

# Timeouts
ClientAliveInterval 300
ClientAliveCountMax 2
LoginGraceTime 60

# Logging
LogLevel VERBOSE

# Strong encryption
Ciphers aes256-gcm@openssh.com,aes128-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512,hmac-sha2-256
\`\`\`

#### SSH Key Management

\`\`\`bash
# Generate strong key
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "user@example.com"

# Deploy to server
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub user@server

# Correct permissions
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

# Test configuration
sshd -t

# Apply changes
systemctl restart sshd
\`\`\`

### Firewall Basics

#### firewalld Quick Reference

\`\`\`bash
# Status
firewall-cmd --state
firewall-cmd --list-all

# Add service
firewall-cmd --add-service=http --permanent
firewall-cmd --add-service=https --permanent
firewall-cmd --reload

# Add port
firewall-cmd --add-port=8080/tcp --permanent
firewall-cmd --reload

# Remove
firewall-cmd --remove-service=http --permanent
firewall-cmd --reload

# Rich rules
firewall-cmd --add-rich-rule='rule family=ipv4 source address=192.168.1.0/24 accept' --permanent
firewall-cmd --reload
\`\`\`

#### iptables Basics

\`\`\`bash
# List rules
iptables -L -n -v

# Allow SSH
iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT

# Allow HTTP/HTTPS
iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -j ACCEPT
iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -j ACCEPT

# Drop all other INPUT
iptables -P INPUT DROP

# Save rules
iptables-save > /etc/iptables/rules.v4
\`\`\`
        `,
        keyPoints: [
          "PermitRootLogin no — root login taqiqlash",
          "ssh-keygen -t ed25519 — zamonaviy SSH key",
          "chmod 700 ~/.ssh, 600 private key",
          "firewall-cmd --permanent --reload"
        ]
